@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+Matching versions against npm-style ranges
+==========================================
+
+A :class:`~semver.Range` uses the range syntax of npm. Comparators in one
+set are separated by spaces and must all match; sets are separated by
+``||`` and at least one must match:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    >>> from semver import Range, satisfies
+    >>> satisfies("1.4.0", "^1.2")
+    True
+    >>> rng = Range("1.x || >=2.5.0")
+    >>> "2.4.0" in rng
+    False
+    >>> str(Range("^1.2"))
+    '>=1.2.0 <2.0.0-0'
+    >>> rng.max_satisfying(["1.0.0", "2.4.0", "3.1.0"])
+    Version(major=3, minor=1, patch=0, prerelease=None, build=None)
+    >>> Range(">1.2.3").min_version()
+    Version(major=1, minor=2, patch=4, prerelease=None, build=None)
+    >>> Range("^1.2").intersects("~1.9")
+    True
+
+Each shorthand expands to primitive comparators. The ``-0`` on an upper
+bound is the lowest prerelease, so the bound excludes that version's
+prereleases too.
+
+X-ranges
+    ``x``, ``X``, ``*`` or a missing part match anything in that place:
+    ``*`` is any version, ``1.x`` is ``>=1.0.0 <2.0.0-0`` and ``1.2`` is
+    ``>=1.2.0 <1.3.0-0``.
+
+Hyphen ranges
+    ``1.2.3 - 2.3.4`` is ``>=1.2.3 <=2.3.4``. A partial upper end accepts
+    everything it starts: ``1.2.3 - 2.3`` is ``>=1.2.3 <2.4.0-0``.
+
+Tilde ranges
+    Patch-level changes, or minor-level ones when no minor is given:
+    ``~1.2.3`` is ``>=1.2.3 <1.3.0-0`` and ``~1`` is ``>=1.0.0 <2.0.0-0``.
+
+Caret ranges
+    Changes that keep the left-most non-zero part: ``^1.2.3`` is
+    ``>=1.2.3 <2.0.0-0``, ``^0.2.3`` is ``>=0.2.3 <0.3.0-0`` and ``^0.0.3``
+    is ``>=0.0.3 <0.0.4-0``.
+
+Primitives
+    ``<``, ``<=``, ``>``, ``>=`` and ``=`` compare with one version:
+    ``>=1.2.3``. On a partial version they round to the whole range it
+    names: ``>1.2`` is ``>=1.3.0`` and ``<=1.2`` is ``<1.3.0-0``.
+
+An invalid expression raises :class:`~semver.InvalidRangeError`, a
+:class:`ValueError`.
+
+
+Prerelease versions
+-------------------
+
+By default a prerelease version such as ``1.2.3-alpha.7`` is only contained
+when a comparator of the same set has a prerelease on the same
+``major.minor.patch``. ``>1.2.3-alpha.3`` contains ``1.2.3-alpha.7`` but not
+``3.4.5-alpha.9``, and ``^1.2.3`` does not contain ``1.5.0-beta.1``.
+Pass ``include_prerelease=True`` to treat prereleases like any other
+version:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    >>> satisfies("1.5.0-beta.1", "^1.2.3")
+    False
+    >>> satisfies("1.5.0-beta.1", "^1.2.3", include_prerelease=True)
+    True
+
+
+Command line
+------------
+
+``pysemver satisfies VERSION RANGE`` prints the version and exits 0 when the
+range contains it, and exits 1 without output when it does not:
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+    $ pysemver satisfies 1.4.0 "^1.2"
+    1.4.0
+
+``pysemver max-satisfying RANGE VERSION [VERSION ...]`` prints the highest
+version the range contains, or exits 1 without output when there is none:
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+    $ pysemver max-satisfying "~1.2" 1.2.0 1.2.9 1.3.0
+    1.2.9
+
+Both take ``--include-prerelease``. An invalid range or version prints
+``ERROR`` and the message on stderr and exits 2.
